#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:52
#: b76e8b1e6cf448bab37f92b9a9f32941
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:53
#: b1a986e693c24fd7b0adf37983482124
msgid "The SBUS pin (SBU), is passed by an inverter to RX2 (UART2 RX), which can be used for all ArduPilot supported receiver protocols, except PPM, CRSF/ELRS, and SRXL2. CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 require the RX2 and TX2s pin be connected instead of the SBUS pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:55
#: 9002a09c27b94800922333dcf0100f8d
msgid "SRXL2 requires :ref:`SERIAL2_OPTIONS<SERIAL2_OPTIONS>` be set to “4”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:56
#: d64a1c1eb500481bb10cb9baa5b9fc64
msgid "Fport should be connected to TX2 via a bi-directional inverter and :ref:`SERIAL2_OPTIONS<SERIAL2_OPTIONS>` be set to “4”. See :ref:`common-connecting-sport-fport`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:58
#: aab1fb5a47b741d8961017941f76e586
msgid "Any UART can also be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot and is compatible with all protocols except PPM (SBUS requires external inversion on other UARTs). See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:61
#: a4719cde3f0c428a8ef63ae5e8305d35
msgid "FrSky Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:62
#: 298ef442d23f45698f16b83ebc950b16
msgid "FrSky Telemetry is supported using the Tx pin of any UART. You need to set the following parameters to enable support for FrSky S.PORT (example shows SERIAL3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:65
#: 580b836242054806af1c00ebf25c92ed
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL3_PROTOCOL<SERIAL3_PROTOCOL>` = 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:66
#: bc676220d8564524bec46860d970cf91
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL3_OPTIONS<SERIAL3_OPTIONS>` = 7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:69
#: 70bc24fa9f2c4987a733e3b906e5a7d1
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:70
#: 9a688ba885374c3f8f9ed952f1205306
msgid "The Droneer F405 supports analog OSD using its integrated MAX7456. Simultaneous HD TVX OSD operation can also be obtained using an available UART whose protocol is set to \"DisplayPort (42)\" and :ref:`OSD_TYPE2<OSD_TYPE2>` set to \"5\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:72
#: c4daa0f539124fdaadcc7a066c7827fa
msgid "The JST-GH-4P connector supports a standard \"Tramp\" VTX connection. Pin 1 of the connector is 10v so be careful not to connect this to a peripheral requiring 5v."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:75
#: 5e97dc53e2cc404785346401b9c075a0
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:76
#: dcf06d8c3ec442e194ac167c060fbf7d
msgid "The Droneer F405 supports up to 9 PWM outputs. The ESC connectors have M1-8 outputs, plus M9(marked LED) for LED strip or another PWM output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:78
#: f284a417064a4cd1bb74acc59efbcd6e
msgid "The PWM is in 3 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:81
#: fe732f7dbb574bfd83d17b3d8e31ff94
msgid "PWM 1-4 in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:82
#: e771231a9392457594a1c7595ee7428d
msgid "PWM 5-8 in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:83
#: 825a2fbeb295482480b1713f0b5c1e2a
msgid "PWM 9 in group3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:85
#: 21e7365f16c64f6c8c9cda28ac96ed1c
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot. Channels 1-4 support bi-directional DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:90
#: 38a6dc62b4e64924a94583c5aa8e2b59
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-DroneerF405.rst:91
#: 58dc83e2c6fa493e8c73b2bdfaf0a7ba
msgid "The board has a internal voltage sensor and connections on the ESC connector for an external current sensor input. The voltage sensor can handle up to 8S LiPo batteries."
msgstr ""

